<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Warszawianka (Whirlwinds of Danger)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">between <a href="/years/1879">1879</a> and <a href="/years/1883">1883</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Warszawianka</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Warszawianka&quot; is a Polish socialist revolutionary song written between 1879 and 1883. Its title, which means a woman of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a> (and can be rendered &quot;The Varsovian&quot; or &quot;The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> of Warsaw&quot;), deliberately recalls an earlier Polish song of the same name; to tell them apart it is often called &quot;Warszawianka of 1905&quot;, after it became the anthem of the workers' protests of the Revolution in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> (1905–1907), when 30 workers were shot at the May Day demonstrations in Warsaw in 1905.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Spanish anarchist writer Valeriano Orobón Fernández wrote the words in the early 1930s, basing them on a German translation of the Polish revolutionary song known as the <b>Warszawianka</b>, whose Polish words Wacław Święcicki had written in the early 1880s and whose music Józef Pławiński had composed.</blockquote><a href="/songs/a-las-barricadas">A las Barricadas</a></li><li><blockquote>After Poland regained independence in 1918 the song became the de facto anthem of the Second Polish Republic and was officially adopted in 1927, ahead of rivals such as &quot;Boże, coś Polskę&quot;, &quot;<b>Warszawianka</b>&quot; and &quot;Rota&quot;.</blockquote><a href="/songs/poland-is-not-yet-lost">Poland Is Not Yet Lost</a></li><li><blockquote>&quot;<b>Warszawianka</b>&quot; is a Polish socialist revolutionary song written between 1879 and 1883.</blockquote><a href="/songs/warszawianka">Warszawianka (Whirlwinds of Danger)</a></li></ul></section>
